---
title: "Session host: one channel across dcserver restarts, host loss and terminate"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Recovery
    lg1: Session
    lg2: Breaks NoOrphanAfterTerminate or NoSessionLoss
    lg3: Breaks NoDoubleSession in some cases
    lg4: Path to the NoDoubleSession or NoOrphanAfterTerminate or NoSessionLoss bug
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 mayBreak
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: No session
  s1: No session, a message waiting
  s2: Creating, a message waiting
  s3: Created, location not yet recorded, a message waiting
  s4: dcserver down, provider still running, a message waiting
  s5: Boot reconcile, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s6: Waiting to re-adopt the created execution, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s7: Waiting to re-adopt the created execution (provider gone), an unrecorded provider running, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s8: Waiting to re-adopt the created execution, two providers running, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s9: Waiting to re-adopt the created execution, two providers running (after the restart)
  s10: Closing the session, two providers running (after the restart)
  s11: Waiting to re-adopt the created execution (provider gone), an unrecorded provider running (after the restart)
  s12: Row closed, provider still running, an unrecorded provider running (after the restart)
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: a message arrives
  s1 --> s2: a message reserves a new execution
  s2 --> s3: the host creates it
  s3 --> s4: dcserver stops
  s4 --> s5: dcserver starts
  s5 --> s6: intake opens
  s6 --> s6: a host probe stops failing
  s6 --> s7: a second create from the same Pending
  s7 --> s8: the host creates it
  s8 --> s8: its pane is recorded
  s8 --> s9: the turn is refused: no provider, or its first prompt already taken
  s9 --> s10: the lone shell is closed
  s10 --> s11: the owned provider is confirmed gone
  s11 --> s12: the recorded pane is gone: row closed
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 teal
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 teal
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 teal
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 teal
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 blue
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 blue
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 blue
  class s6 bugPath
  class s7 blue
  class s7 bugPath
  class s8 blue
  class s8 mayBreak
  class s8 bugPath
  class s9 blue
  class s9 bugPath
  class s10 blue
  class s10 bugPath
  class s11 blue
  class s11 bugPath
  class s12 teal
  class s12 breaks
  class s12 bugPath
